{"id":"periyar","name":"Periyar Memorial House","category":"Heritage & Culture","location":"Periyar Street, Erode","description":"A memorial in the ancestral home of social reformer E. V. Ramasamy, preserving the story of his life and public work.","tagline":"A reformer’s legacy","note":"Confirm visiting hours locally; photography inside may be restricted.","source":"https://erode.nic.in/heritage-tourism/","image":"/__l5e/assets-v1/2df54ca0-9269-4de0-a1e7-04ca089ad115/erode-periyar.jpg","mapQuery":"Periyar Memorial House, Periyar Street, Erode, Tamil Nadu, India","ordinality":14},
{"id":"kodumanal","name":"Kodumanal Archaeological Site","category":"Heritage & Culture","location":"Kodumanal, near the Noyyal River","description":"An ancient trade and industrial settlement known for bead-making, iron working and archaeological evidence of far-reaching trade.","tagline":"Ancient stories","note":"An archaeological site, not a daily visitor attraction. Seek permission and current access information; never disturb remains.","source":"https://erode.nic.in/heritage-tourism/","image":"/__l5e/assets-v1/abd6b502-addf-45f3-aa30-8a0af081fc89/erode-kodumanal.jpg","mapQuery":"Kodumanal Archaeological Site, Kodumanal, near the Noyyal River, Tamil Nadu, India","ordinality":15},
{"id":"voc","name":"VOC Park","category":"Leisure & Parks","location":"Erode city","description":"A well-known public recreation space in Erode for a leisurely walk and an easy-going break within the city.","tagline":"A city pause","note":"Facilities and accessible areas can change. Confirm current park access locally.","source":"https://erode.nic.in/tourism/places-of-interest/","image":"/__l5e/assets-v1/20139ca7-21f2-4a73-8aac-b26207fbeeeb/erode-voc.jpg","mapQuery":"VOC Park, Erode city, Tamil Nadu, India","photoSource":"https://erodeinfo.com/erode-photos/erode-voc-park-photos.htm","photoCredit":"Erode Info","ordinality":16},
{"id":"kalingarayan","name":"Kalingarayan Canal and Anicut","category":"Dams & Rivers","location":"Bhavani and the Erode countryside","description":"A historic irrigation system drawing from the Bhavani River, reflecting the engineering heritage of the Kongu region.","tagline":"Engineering heritage","note":"The canal spans multiple places; the map link points to the anicut. Keep clear of flowing water.","source":"https://erode.nic.in/water-bodies-dams/","image":"/__l5e/assets-v1/ccb76410-28d4-47ac-b43f-54e40ec1e314/erode-kalingarayan.jpg","mapQuery":"Kalingarayan Anicut Bhavani Tamil Nadu","ordinality":17},
